    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d721-a5">

                <pb facs="0689" n="591" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg591"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Subinclosure 4.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >New York</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-01-19"><hi rendition="#italic">January 19,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>I, the undersigned, do solemnly swear that I am the shipper of the
                    within-mentioned goods, to wit: One hundred cases, each containing two 5–gallon
                    tins, of cotton-seed oil, placed on board the steamship <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Maria</hi> for delivery at Delagoa Bay. That the merchandise was shipped in
                    good faith to Patlansky Brothers, British subjects, residing at Johannesburg, S.
                    A. R., and that the draft against said merchandise went to protest.</p>
                <p>That the within-mentioned invoice, $492.77, represents actual cost to-day and
                    does not cover expenses of protest, cablegrams, etc., and that I am a lawful
                    citizen of the United States of America.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">R. W. Geldart</hi></signed>.</closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">State of New York</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">City and County of New York:</hi></p>
                    <p>Sworn to and subscribed to before me this 19th day of January, 1900.</p>
                    <closer>[<hi rendition="#small-caps">seal.</hi>] <signed><hi
                                rendition="#small-caps">Tho. Nash.</hi></signed></closer>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
